From b7ef503bb3053a2fbad0c471ad347b4077374ba4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SP11 Linux Project <272055834+geocausa@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 21:06:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 29/47] ASoC: qcom: restore Denali protected pull graph
 lifecycle

Keep the qualified FullIO speaker graph resident across ALSA
STOP/prepare, configure pull transport before protected formats, and
restore the captured client-scoped subgraph management order without
changing generic graphs.

Give the protected graph its own coherent uncached position mapping
and validate DMA pointer reads. Match the new position and client
management transactions by opcode and token; retain graph DMA rather
than free it after an uncertain close/unmap. Preserve the existing
soft-pause implementation, Windows-full calibration, and closed
unified5 fixes.

Provenance: geocausa/SP11X1e-audio at
3232e1dacdeb580a10a9cb8d4756a4518a7bd83e,
repro/golden-v32/source-overlay/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/ plus FullIO
production records. Oaklee v7.3 corroboration and narrowly adapted
request/timeout guards: ooaklee/linux_ms_dev_kit-sp11 at
294b383083125342ff5837957bf28328859d03db,
q6apm.c/q6apm.h/q6apm-dai.c.

Based on the unified5 UNMAP response-opcode checkpoint. Static: git
diff --check; strict checkpatch 0 errors/warnings/checks. Physical
audio and system suspend are untested for this source candidate.

Signed-off-by: SP11 Linux Project <272055834+geocausa@users.noreply.github.com>
